-- הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 "תשלום קצובת נסיעה", מהדורה 10 (1.5.2025)
-- Edition 10 of the Accountant-General's travel-allowance instruction,
-- updated for new tariffs and the new payroll systems: the tickets are
-- "משולב מלא" (bus, train and local train), a move is reported through the
-- personal portal, the three-yearly refresh and annex B's payroll codes are
-- gone, and the tax is grossed up above 684 shekels a month whatever the
-- week. What it repeats from edition 9 it takes from that file by import.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `kitzuvat-nesia-common`
IMPORT `2024-08-08_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v9`

-- Tariffs: the notice's, inputs (`travel fares`), now the "משולב מלא"
-- tickets. No rule here rounds (convention rounding.default).

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: ‘משרה מלאה’ here is
-- the blind employee's basis for the allowance (five times the monthly
-- ticket, 2.3.7), not the hours of work and rest.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: ‘בעל’ here is the holder of a
-- post or of a service or assigned car (‘בעל רכב צמוד’, ‘בעל נהג צמוד’),
-- not a husband; the instruction sets one travel allowance for every
-- employee, man or woman, and does not distinguish between them.

-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: ‘חודש סיום העסקה’ here is a
-- month in which the travel allowance is paid pro rata (2.1.5), not notice
-- of dismissal or resignation.

§ `הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 תשלום קצובת נסיעה — מהדורה 10`

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- 1.1, as in edition 9.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1
GIVEN `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `edition 10 applies to` `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IF
    `edition 9 applies to` `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit`

-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 Further payments in Eilat and the Negev are the notice "תשלומים לנוסעים / עובדים באילת ותוספת ערבה", which the corpus does not hold; no rule here.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/p2 The instruction's purpose; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-4 A pointer to annex A, whose definitions the rules below cite; no rule.

§§ `2.1 זכאות לקצובת נסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 The heading "זכאות לקצובת נסיעה"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.1.1, 2.2.1 and its cases, annex A's definitions 1 and 7, as in edition 9.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_7 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-4 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 10` m IF
    `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 9` m

-- 2.1.2 and annex A's definition 4, as in edition 9: one residence.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4
`the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 10` MEANS `the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 9`

-- 2.1.3, in edition 9's words: one single trip a week from the workplace to
-- the permanent home. Annex B and its code 1360, which paid two, are gone,
-- and the clause is read as it is printed.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
`the trips home a week, edition 10` MEANS 1

-- 2.1.4-2.1.6 and annex A's definitions 2-3 ("חופשי יומי – משולב מלא",
-- "חופשי חודשי – משולב מלא": bus, train and local train), as in edition 9.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-4
`the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 10` MEANS
    `the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 9`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5__pnt_2-1-5-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5__pnt_2-1-5-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 10` f m IS
    `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 9` f m

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-6
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 10` amount m IS
    `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 9` amount m

§§ `2.3 קביעת זכאות לקצובת נסיעה בעקבות רפורמת דרך שווה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.3.1-2.3.3, as in edition 9 (the means now "bus, train, local train,
-- cable car or a combination of them in a partial or full combined ticket").
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-2
`the train is refunded with every other means of public transport, edition 10` MEANS
    `the train is refunded with every other means of public transport, edition 9`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-3
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`, `the equalisation the notice sets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 10` m `the equalisation the notice sets` IS
    `the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 9` m `the equalisation the notice sets`

-- 2.3.4, as in edition 9: a cap of 1,330 shekels a month.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-4
`the monthly cap, edition 10` MEANS `the monthly cap, edition 9`

-- 2.3.5-2.3.6 and annex A's definition 5, as in edition 9.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance for travel to work, edition 10` f m IS
    `the allowance for travel to work, edition 9` f m

-- 2.3.7 and annex A's definition 6, as in edition 9; whether 2.3.4's cap
-- binds it the edition still does not say
-- (F-2025-05-01_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v10-a). The reading adopted
-- (convention precedence.specific), as edition 9's: not capped.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7/p3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_6
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the blind employee's allowance, edition 10` f m IS
    `the blind employee's allowance, edition 9` f m

`a blind employee's five tickets of 300 pass the cap, edition 10` MEANS
    5 TIMES 300 GREATER THAN `the monthly cap, edition 10`
#ASSERT `a blind employee's five tickets of 300 pass the cap, edition 10`

-- 2.3.8, as in edition 9: 128 shekels a month in addition.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-8 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-8/p2
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 10` m IS
    `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 9` m

§§ `2.4 קצובה בגין נסיעה בשבתות וחגים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.4.1-2.4.3, as in edition 9: the daily ticket doubled for each Sabbath
-- or holiday day the employee came, within the cap with the monthly
-- allowance.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 10` f m IS
    `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 9` f m

-- The month's allowance, as edition 9 builds it, with one trip home a week.
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance, edition 10` f m IS
    IF NOT `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 10` m THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the blind employee's allowance, edition 10` f m
         WHEN JUST b THEN b
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 10` f m
            PLUS `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 10` m
            PLUS `the weekly trips to the permanent home` f m `the trips home a week, edition 10`

§§ `2.5 דיווח על כתובת מגורים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.5.1-2.5.2: an employee who changed residence or workplace updates the
-- new address in the personal portal and attaches the form "קצובת נסיעה";
-- the information goes to human resources, who pass it to the salary unit
-- for the updated payment. One who did not report it so has every payment
-- difference collected retroactively from the day of the move. The
-- three-yearly refresh of edition 9's 2.5.2 is gone.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `reporting a move, edition 10` IS
    PARTY `the government employee`
    MUST  `update the address in the personal portal and attach the travel-allowance form`
    HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pass the report to the salary unit`
           HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
                  MUST  `pay the updated travel allowance`))
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MAY   `collect the payment differences retroactively`)

§§ `2.6 יישום במערכות השכר`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.6.1: paid through the payroll system, by the notice's directions.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `paying through the payroll, edition 10` IS `paying through the payroll, edition 9`

§§ `2.7 ניכוי מס הכנסה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.7.1, as in edition 9.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `withholding income tax, edition 10` IS `withholding income tax, edition 9`

-- 2.7.2: the tax is grossed up on the part of the allowance above 684
-- shekels a month, whatever the employee's week.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-2
`the gross-up threshold, edition 10` MEANS 684

GIVEN allowance IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part grossed up, edition 10` allowance IS
    `the part above` allowance `the gross-up threshold, edition 10`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-2
GIVEN allowance IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `grossing up the tax, edition 10` allowance IS
    IF `the part grossed up, edition 10` allowance GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `gross up the tax on the travel allowance` `part`
               PROVIDED `part` EQUALS `the part grossed up, edition 10` allowance
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `3-4 מסמכים ישימים ונספחים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-2 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-3 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-4 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-5 The applicable documents (the takshir's chapters 28.3 and 16.6, the form, the two notices); a source list, no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2 The list of annexes; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 Annex A's title "הגדרות"; its definitions are cited by the rules that use them.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 akn:att_2__hc_1/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1/t1 Annex B, the table of the editions' changes; a record, no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

`placeholder fares, edition 10` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 300
        `daily free pass`       IS 20
        `single fare`           IS 15
        `intercity single fare` IS 0

`edition 10 pays` m MEANS `the travel allowance, edition 10` `placeholder fares, edition 10` m

#ASSERT `edition 10 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) EQUALS 300

-- 2.1.3 as printed: four weeks of one single trip home at 15, in addition.
`a relocated employee's month, edition 10` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 4 0
#ASSERT `edition 10 pays` `a relocated employee's month, edition 10` EQUALS 360

-- 2.7.2: an allowance of 900 is grossed up on 216; one of 600 on nothing.
#ASSERT `the part grossed up, edition 10` 900 EQUALS 216
#ASSERT `the part grossed up, edition 10` 600 EQUALS 0
